From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 18:28:12 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: surface-laptop8: Disable the Wi-Fi hardware
 rfkill

The WCN7850 hardware rfkill input on the Surface Laptop 8 reads as
"radio off" and the OS cannot control it, so ath12k leaves Wi-Fi
hard-blocked. Set disable-rfkill on the Wi-Fi node, as the Surface Pro
11 does.

Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-microsoft-surface-laptop8.dts | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-microsoft-surface-laptop8.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-microsoft-surface-laptop8.dts
index 4b99b702924..d2fcc4c4306 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-microsoft-surface-laptop8.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/glymur-microsoft-surface-laptop8.dts
@@ -716,6 +716,9 @@ &pcie4_port0 {
 	wifi@0 {
 		compatible = "pci17cb,1107";
 		reg = <0x10000 0x0 0x0 0x0 0x0>;
+
+		/* The WCN7850's hardware rfkill input reads as "radio off". */
+		disable-rfkill;
 	};
 };
 
-- 
